ack vs pre-rendering for published document paths — DECIDED: SPA fallback, because the manifest is deploy-time state under <stateRoot>, not build input, so pre-rendering would invert the publication direction (every publish needing a website redeploy), break epic Law 6, and give the content root a second writer. Written up in /home/err/spaces/foresight/website/docs/decisions/0001-spa-fallback-over-prerendering.md with the three costs and their mitigations (client-rendered PublishedNotFound view, runtime robots noindex, html-response-means-absent at the fetch edge), and a confirmed-by-curl note that a deep path is answered with the DEFAULT locale's shell until JS corrects lang. Linked from AGENTS.md and README.md.\",\n    \"Assets are staged, never symlinked — recorded in /home/err/spaces/foresight/website/AGENTS.md section 'Assets are staged, never symlinked' and in README.md 'Gallery assets': the two committed absolute symlinks are gone and gitignored, roots come from OPENHAX_GRAPHICS_ROOT / OPENHAX_MUSIC_ROOT (defaulting to the original paths so the author's workflow is unchanged), the gallery manifest is regenerated FROM WHAT WAS STAGED, and zero staged assets is an explicitly valid build.\",\n    \"The three Foresight invariants are now actually stated in /home/err/spaces/foresight/website/AGENTS.md, one section each with the enforcing test named: :website/copy-resolves-from-locale-dictionaries, :website/published-artifact-is-static, :website/translations-are-reviewed-upstream.\",\n    \"One build output directory (finding #1 against services#19) — recorded in AGENTS.md under :website/published-artifact-is-static and in the shadow-cljs.edn header comment: dist/site is the single docroot for both :dev-http and release, replacing dist/cljs + dist/app.css + a root index.html + three merged dev roots.\",\n    \"The reader's own manifest expectation is declared in /home/err/spaces/foresight/website/src/cljc/open_hax/website/law/published_manifest.cljc as the website's side of the contract (a rules table in the docstring), explicitly not a copy of the writer's schema, with the Knoxx writer named for provenance.\",\n    \"Namespace architecture recorded as a table in AGENTS.md (shape / domain / law / data pure in .cljc; infra / extern / views / build effectful in .cljs), plus the zero-warnings rule.\"\n  ],\n  \"blocked_or_deferred\": [\n    \"No browser verification. The agent-browser skill's CLI is not installed in this environment ('agent-browser: command not found') and there is no headless browser available, so I never loaded the app in a real browser. I substituted the strongest available runtime evidence: test/cljs/open_hax/website/render_test.cljs drives the real components through react-dom/server and asserts on the actual markup (French hero, translated tags with untranslated product names, interpolated year, switcher hrefs, empty listing renders \\\"\\\", loud alert). I also served dist/site over HTTP and curled it, and separately curled shadow-cljs :dev-http (/, /es/, /ja/, /de/, /es/notes/hello, /pt/, /cljs/app.js, /app.css, /favicon.svg all 200; /published/manifest.edn 404 = the absent case). What remains unverified is client-side behaviour after hydration: the popstate handler, the runtime lang correction, the robots noindex meta and the artifact fetch have unit-level coverage but no live browser run.\",\n    \"The CI workflow has never executed (no push permitted, no Actions runner here). See the CARD 2 DoD entry.\",\n    \"The Knoxx writer namespace in the fixture provenance comments (knoxx.backend.infra.publication-target-static-site) is a FORWARD REFERENCE. It does not exist on knoxx main or on feat/publication-artifact-contract — only the sibling publication-target-memory does. The comments name the card (knoxx-publication-static-site-target) alongside it so the pointer stays useful if the name changes.\",\n    \"Asset staging could only be proven with a synthetic library. Both real roots are unusable on this 